    "body": "Parent programme: #820\n\n## Objective\n\nRepresent supervised instruction behavior as versioned, provenance-bound graph evidence and serve it through generic, deterministic patch semantics without erasing base capabilities.\n\n## Current evidence\n\n- R4G1 already contains patch-capable structures, but patch presence is not the same as normative production R4Engine reachability.\n- The live ledger currently overstates R4G1Runtime patch ownership as serving reachability.\n- A fixed 75% adherence target without task strata, retention, baselines, or confidence is not a sufficient admission contract.\n\n## Entry criteria\n\nS1 prompt causality and S2 selective risk are promoted; S3/S4 establish the generation/planning scopes that instruction claims may invoke.\n\n## Native dependencies\n\nBlocked by #826 and #823.\n\n## Promotion gate\n\nOn unseen templates and held-out tasks, delta covers meet frozen capability and retention thresholds, are causally attributable to the overlay, match or beat an equal-data full recompile under declared budgets, and execute through the normative serving path.\n\n## Kill / redesign criterion\n\nIf delta overlays cannot match the full-recompile control or materially damage retained capabilities, keep instruction data in full compilation and do not promote hot-patch alignment.\n\n## Native children\n\n- [ ] #847 — Freeze instruction/retention benchmarks and record semantics\n- [ ] #848 — Integrate production PTCH/RTNX and A/B delta covers\n- [ ] #849 — Bind serving admission to capability and retention evidence\n\nGitHub's native parent/sub-issue relationship is the hierarchy source of truth.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Encode privileged hidden prompts or inference-time network dependencies.\n- Claim broad alignment from aggregate adherence alone.\n\n## Repository conformance\n\nPrimary IDs: RF-09, RF-22, RF-23; add patch-lifecycle/instruction IDs only when built. Patch activation, precedence, provenance, rollback, and witness attribution must be normative and fail closed.\n\nEvery leaf declares execution scope, preserves the applicable P-4/determinism/allocation/no_std/error/witness contracts, maps to existing RF capabilities or justifies a new one, and updates generated conformance only through its TOML/Gherkin/test sources. Empirical work posts the repository run contract before expensive execution.\n\n## Closure rule\n\nClose only after every native child has a completed, negative, not-triggered, or explicitly descoped verdict and this tracker records `PROMOTE`, `REVISE`, `LIMIT`, or `RETIRE` with exact evidence links.",
